   "id": 511043,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A position vs. time graph of a frog swimming across a pond has two distinct straight-line sections. The slope of the first section is <span data-math=\"1\\,\\text{m/s}\">1\\,\\text{m/s}</span>. The slope of the second section is <span data-math=\"0\\,\\text{m/s}\">0\\,\\text{m/s}</span>. If each section lasts <span data-math=\"1\\,\\text{second}\">1\\,\\text{second}</span>, then what is the frog’s total average velocity?",
